    "['mpls traffic-eng area [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ospf traffic-engineering', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ospf traffic-engineering', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for `mpls traffic-eng area 0`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ospf traffic-engineering\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, enabling MPLS traffic engineering for OSPF is done with a single global command under OSPF (`traffic-engineering`), rather than specifying an area. The area-specific functionality is implied since OSPF must be configured for the appropriate areas elsewhere in the configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ospf traffic-engineering'}]]": 1,
